      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T18:24:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not against this CL since I don\u0027t have the full context on why we need it, and I don\u0027t think this CL introduces new bugs.\n\nJFYI, the old implementation was only used to handle the VkFence where the guest exports a sync fd, i.e. `vkGetFenceFdKHR`. It was never intended to cover the guest `vkWaitForFences` case. The guest application should guarantee the synchronization between `vkWaitForFences` and `vkQueueSubmit`. And Vulkan spec doesn\u0027t require host synchronization between `vkWaitForFences` calls, so we don\u0027t need synchronization between the host `vkWaitForFences` that implements the guest `vkGetFenceFdKHR`(this function), and the host `vkWaitForFences` that implements the guest `vkWaitForFencces`(because on the host, they are essentially 2 `vkWaitForFences`).",
      "revId": "0a8d9d74fd9ec36ba1ee1f64d3096f489f4f7edb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
